From 7aa448600e787428e64fbeec70040449eb27c0b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:38:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 62/68] Demo page and Developer tools: the identity verdict
 follows the test face, a check always ends, the overrides shown are the ones
 that run, the models' load state, and TalkBack roles (task 29)

Review fixes (debug and profile builds only), each with a widget test that failed on the old page:
- W1: a test face enrolled or deleted on Developer tools left the old verdict ("Same person") and note
  ("Enrolled - now anyone can use 2. Check identity") on the demo page. A changed enrolment time now clears them.
- W3: verifyIdentity throwing anything but a PlatformException, or the identity override failing to switch off,
  left the page "Checking..." with every control disabled (and the override possibly on, so every identity check
  of this process, the real sign-in's included, used the test face). Both are caught; a failed switch-off says to
  restart the app before signing in. The debug page's identity check had the same pattern: fixed the same way.
- W2: the debug page started its switches from defaults while the native overrides set by the demo page (fake
  scenario, forced challenges) stayed active: it showed PASS_ACTIVE and ran ENGINE_ERROR. Its controls now start
  from the recorded overrides (LivenessDevOverrides), so what they show is what runs. A hot restart still resets
  the Dart record while the native side keeps its overrides (developer only; not fixable without a native list).
- W4: a bundle that fails verification never loads, and the page said "Models loading..." for good. While the
  version reads '', it is read again every 2 s; after 30 s the page says "Models not loaded".
- W5: the run cards, the simulated rows and Developer tools are buttons with an enabled state for TalkBack (they
  were plain tap targets: disabled while busy, with nothing said), and the identity verdict and the result panel
  are live regions.

flutter test test/liveness: 330 passing, 20 skipped (325 + 5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
